269
00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:24.140
He thinks you're therapy.

270
00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:27.810
He figures,
if two babies can hammer me
into a psycho ward,

271
00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:29.790
what'll l do with this?

272
00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:32.310
He's so stupid.

273
00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:35.860
He thinks he pulled me
through the breakdown

274
00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:37.920
when it was only Christy.

275
00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:40.300
Always. Only Chris.

276
00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:41.990
Jesus.

277
00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:44.800
l was looking through
his postcards.

278
00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:47.000
Paintings were his obsession.

279
00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:50.440
He used art
as another way to love me,
to help me.

280
00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:53.600
To keep us always together.

281
00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.750
CHRIS: Annie.

282
00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.110
l'm here, babe.

283
00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:02.840
l still exist.

284
00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:07.120
You're thinking of me.

285
00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.290
Keep thinking of me.

286
00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:12.290
Come on, with me.

287
00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:15.070
You were always with me.

288
00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:18.870
The people who finished
each other's sentences.
Remember us?

289
00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:24.000
l still exist.

290
00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:27.570
l still exist!

291
00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:32.880
l still exist.

292
00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:36.880
Just write it down.

293
00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:40.920
Write it down.

294
00:21:44.930 --> 00:21:46.520
"This is Chris."

295
00:21:47.730 --> 00:21:49.500
(ANNIE SIGHING)

296
00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:51.960
"This is Chris."

297
00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:00.100
"l

298
00:22:02.820 --> 00:22:04.080
"still

299
00:22:08.020 --> 00:22:09.280
"exist."

300
00:22:20.330 --> 00:22:21.560
Read it.

301
00:22:22.470 --> 00:22:23.700
Read it.

302
00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:56.490
(ANNIE SOBBING)

303
00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:01.670
CHRIS:
Christ, when does it end?

304
00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:04.970
DOC: There's no rules, Chris.

305
00:23:05.240 --> 00:23:07.110
lt ends when you want.

306
00:23:07.910 --> 00:23:09.180
Where were you?

307
00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:10.770
Someplace else.

308
00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:14.520
You think l'm a figment
of your imagination?

309
00:23:14.590 --> 00:23:16.610
lt's real.
She's real.
You're real.

310
00:23:16.690 --> 00:23:17.990
lt's all real.

311
00:23:18.060 --> 00:23:20.390
That's the point
if there is one.

312
00:23:21.490 --> 00:23:24.400
lt's over when you stop
wanting to hurt her.

313
00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:38.770
(ANNIE SNIFFLING)

314
00:23:41.450 --> 00:23:42.680
Forever.

315
00:23:54.730 --> 00:23:56.390
Don't worry, baby.

316
00:23:58.460 --> 00:24:00.490
l'm not leaving you alone.

317
00:24:01.070 --> 00:24:02.300
l'm not going anywhere.

318
00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:03.730
(SCREAMING)

319
00:24:07.170 --> 00:24:08.440
(SOBBING)

320
00:24:24.490 --> 00:24:25.980
Goodbye, babe.

321
00:24:30.960 --> 00:24:32.230
(SIGHING)

322
00:24:54.990 --> 00:24:56.580
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

323
00:25:11.300 --> 00:25:13.070
(lNSECTS CHITTERING)

324
00:25:34.560 --> 00:25:35.930
(CHUCKLING)

325
00:25:38.600 --> 00:25:40.070
(DOG BARKING)

326
00:25:53.050 --> 00:25:54.880
Katie, it's you!

327
00:25:56.110 --> 00:25:57.840
You're young again!

328
00:25:58.820 --> 00:25:59.980
Katie!

329
00:26:02.220 --> 00:26:03.690
Come here, Katie.

330
00:26:03.760 --> 00:26:05.090
(LAUGHING)

331
00:26:06.760 --> 00:26:07.920
Katie.

332
00:26:11.400 --> 00:26:12.860
Come on, hey!

333
00:26:12.970 --> 00:26:14.430
(KATIE BARKING)

334
00:26:14.500 --> 00:26:16.160
Boy, l screwed up.

335
00:26:17.170 --> 00:26:18.830
l'm in dog heaven.

336
00:26:28.950 --> 00:26:32.210
A place where we all go
can't be bad, can it, girl?

337
00:27:00.380 --> 00:27:03.310
Maybe l'm not in your heaven
after all, girl!

338
00:27:03.580 --> 00:27:05.070
Maybe you're in mine!

339
00:27:05.150 --> 00:27:06.620
(KATIE BARKS)

340
00:27:12.490 --> 00:27:14.930
Annie!

341
00:27:35.210 --> 00:27:36.580
(SQUISHING)

342
00:27:48.730 --> 00:27:51.290
DOC: Chris, what the hell
have you done?

343
00:27:51.360 --> 00:27:53.890
That's not how
you use a stethoscope!

344
00:27:54.270 --> 00:27:55.670
Albert Lewis?

345
00:27:55.730 --> 00:28:00.500
Last time you saw me
l was 63, stretched out
on a cardiac ward!

346
00:28:00.570 --> 00:28:01.560
(LAUGHING)

347
00:28:01.640 --> 00:28:03.940
You thought l was old
and decrepit, huh?

348
00:28:04.010 --> 00:28:06.310
Talking about
"Ah, can't go on!"

349
00:28:08.080 --> 00:28:10.710
Who wants to be 63
throughout eternity?

350
00:28:11.020 --> 00:28:12.250
Look at you on the water!

351
00:28:12.320 --> 00:28:14.620
Well, hello! Come on.

352
00:28:15.320 --> 00:28:18.310
Walk along, feel the beat!

353
00:28:18.460 --> 00:28:20.080
Dancing on water!

354
00:28:20.390 --> 00:28:21.920
Smooth as ever!

355
00:28:23.600 --> 00:28:25.220
And that was you,

356
00:28:26.300 --> 00:28:29.360
just now, when l died.

357
00:28:30.300 --> 00:28:33.970
l thought you recognized me,
because you called me "Doc".

358
00:28:34.170 --> 00:28:36.270
Me being your favorite doc.

359
00:28:36.610 --> 00:28:41.600
Could you lend me a hand?
l'm up to my ass
in problems again, Chief.

360
00:28:42.550 --> 00:28:44.680
Oh, Chris.

361
00:28:46.890 --> 00:28:48.220
Come here.

362
00:28:49.320 --> 00:28:51.310
You are still kinda ugly.

363
00:28:53.490 --> 00:28:55.590
You taught me a lot, Chief.

364
00:28:55.860 --> 00:28:57.020
Nice place you got here.

365
00:28:57.100 --> 00:28:59.890
No, no.
Nice place you got here.

366
00:29:00.300 --> 00:29:01.290
Me?

367
00:29:01.370 --> 00:29:03.560
Sure,
you're making all this.

368
00:29:04.100 --> 00:29:08.540
We're insecure at first,
so we need
safety and comfort.

369
00:29:08.770 --> 00:29:10.740
We all paint
our surroundings, Chris.

370
00:29:10.810 --> 00:29:13.940
But you're
the first guy l know
to use real paint!

371
00:29:14.010 --> 00:29:16.610
There's so much here
she didn't paint.

372
00:29:18.520 --> 00:29:20.040
Like that bird.

373
00:29:21.390 --> 00:29:24.690
Annie gave you a start,
like holding onto handrails.

374
00:29:24.920 --> 00:29:26.950
You're creating a world.

375
00:29:27.290 --> 00:29:31.290
From your imagination,
from paintings you love,
anything you want.

376
00:29:31.760 --> 00:29:33.530
Why doesn't it move?

377
00:29:33.730 --> 00:29:35.830
lt will
when you want it to.

378
00:29:39.940 --> 00:29:41.300
(SQUAWKING)

379
00:29:42.840 --> 00:29:45.070
Oh-hoh! You go, boy!

380
00:29:45.140 --> 00:29:46.170
Can l make it dive?

381
00:29:46.240 --> 00:29:47.770
You're the painter now!

382
00:29:47.850 --> 00:29:49.440
lt's your world.

383
00:29:49.550 --> 00:29:51.180
(CHRIS SCREAMING)

384
00:29:51.850 --> 00:29:53.180
(WHOOPING)

385
00:29:54.020 --> 00:29:55.510
Look at it go!

386
00:29:56.860 --> 00:29:58.850
How about turquoise wings?

387
00:29:58.920 --> 00:30:00.260
Turquoise!

388
00:30:00.330 --> 00:30:03.230
And a little mauve,
all right!

389
00:30:03.360 --> 00:30:04.990
(ALBERT WHOOPING)

390
00:30:19.810 --> 00:30:21.440
l didn't do that.

391
00:30:21.580 --> 00:30:22.810
No, l did.

392
00:30:22.880 --> 00:30:25.780
When we're together
it's like dual controls.

393
00:30:26.050 --> 00:30:28.040
Can l make elephants fly?

394
00:30:29.250 --> 00:30:31.350
Didn't Annie paint a house?

395
00:30:36.390 --> 00:30:38.660
Yeah, it's our dream house.

396
00:30:41.700 --> 00:30:43.930
Just a stroll
across the water.

397
00:30:45.270 --> 00:30:47.100
Let's take the shortcut.

398
00:30:51.910 --> 00:30:53.040
Nice shortcut.

399
00:30:53.110 --> 00:30:54.980
lt's easy, look at me!

400
00:30:55.210 --> 00:30:56.270
l'm gonna drown.

401
00:30:56.350 --> 00:30:58.980
ALBERT: You can't.
You're already dead.

402
00:30:59.280 --> 00:31:02.150
Oh. Am l...
Am l really here?

403
00:31:03.020 --> 00:31:05.050
What do you mean by "you"?

404
00:31:05.120 --> 00:31:07.250
Are you your arm
or your leg?

405
00:31:07.490 --> 00:31:09.360
Partly.
Really?

406
00:31:09.730 --> 00:31:11.820
And if you lost your limbs?

407
00:31:12.030 --> 00:31:13.590
l'd still be me.

408
00:31:13.670 --> 00:31:15.290
What is the "me"?

409
00:31:15.830 --> 00:31:17.360
My brain, l suppose.

410
00:31:17.440 --> 00:31:18.700
Your brain?

411
00:31:18.770 --> 00:31:20.800
Your brain is a body part.

412
00:31:20.970 --> 00:31:22.800
Like your fingernail
or your heart.

413
00:31:22.870 --> 00:31:24.900
Why is that the part
that's you?

414
00:31:25.880 --> 00:31:29.310
Because "l" is sort of
a voice in my head.

415
00:31:29.380 --> 00:31:31.650
The part that thinks,
that feels.

416
00:31:31.720 --> 00:31:33.810
That is aware that l exist.

417
00:31:39.690 --> 00:31:43.250
So if you're aware you exist,
then you do.

418
00:31:44.330 --> 00:31:46.530
That's why you're still here.

419
00:31:48.930 --> 00:31:50.460
(KATIE BARKING)

420
00:31:50.540 --> 00:31:51.870
(LAUGHING)

421
00:32:00.310 --> 00:32:03.680
ALBERT: No windows.
What aren't you ready to see,
l wonder?

422
00:32:07.950 --> 00:32:10.750
Drink it.
Think it's coffee
and it will be.

423
00:32:11.190 --> 00:32:12.180
(SIGHING)

424
00:32:12.290 --> 00:32:13.380
Okay.

425
00:32:14.190 --> 00:32:15.590
lt's coffee.

426
00:32:17.860 --> 00:32:19.520
Paint! Acrylic.

427
00:32:20.430 --> 00:32:21.460
(CHUCKLING)

428
00:32:21.530 --> 00:32:23.190
Why is it so hard?

429
00:32:23.270 --> 00:32:24.430
What?

430
00:32:24.600 --> 00:32:26.300
Your brain is meat.

431
00:32:26.370 --> 00:32:28.270
lt rots and disappears.

432
00:32:29.010 --> 00:32:31.700
You thought
that's all there was to you?

433
00:32:34.050 --> 00:32:36.240
Like you're
in your house now.

434
00:32:36.720 --> 00:32:40.240
You're in your house,
it doesn't mean
you are your house.

435
00:32:40.320 --> 00:32:42.810
The house falls down,
you walk away.

436
00:32:44.820 --> 00:32:46.550
But l rebuilt, huh?

437
00:32:46.630 --> 00:32:49.150
You see your body
because you like seeing one.

438
00:32:49.230 --> 00:32:51.660
We're seeing
what we choose to see.

439
00:32:53.500 --> 00:32:55.520
Let me show you something.

440
00:33:19.120 --> 00:33:20.110
Ha!

441
00:33:27.900 --> 00:33:30.430
CHRIS: lt's real.
Where is the paint?

442
00:33:30.770 --> 00:33:34.540
ALBERT:
You don't need it anymore.
This is your world now.

443
00:33:37.710 --> 00:33:39.300
Thought is real.

444
00:33:39.680 --> 00:33:41.670
Physical is the illusion.

445
00:33:43.010 --> 00:33:44.410
lronic, huh?

446
00:33:48.390 --> 00:33:50.290
Where's God in all this?

447
00:33:50.360 --> 00:33:51.850
He's up there.

448
00:33:52.590 --> 00:33:53.680
Somewhere.

449
00:33:53.760 --> 00:33:55.730
Shouting down
that he loves us.

450
00:33:55.790 --> 00:33:57.690
Wondering why
we can't hear him.

451
00:33:57.760 --> 00:33:59.090
You think?

452
00:34:01.330 --> 00:34:02.990
Drink your coffee.

453
00:34:05.500 --> 00:34:06.660
Needs milk.

454
00:34:06.740 --> 00:34:08.540
Don't push your luck.

455
00:34:15.450 --> 00:34:16.940
(BIRDS CAWING)

456
00:34:22.420 --> 00:34:24.820
ANNIE:
What do you think, Christy?

457
00:34:27.430 --> 00:34:28.790
Right here.

458
00:34:31.300 --> 00:34:33.960
Like this? You think?

459
00:34:50.750 --> 00:34:53.270
They say
we live in our minds anyway.

460
00:34:55.690 --> 00:34:59.990
Having you with me,
like this, keeps me happy.

461
00:35:03.460 --> 00:35:05.790
Why do l believe
you can hear me?

462
00:35:07.230 --> 00:35:09.530
Why do l think
you can see this?

463
00:35:15.170 --> 00:35:18.270
CHRIS:
What's that purple tree?
l never saw that.

464
00:35:19.710 --> 00:35:21.270
Let's take a look.

465
00:35:21.350 --> 00:35:23.250
Think you can get there
in eight seconds?

466
00:35:23.310 --> 00:35:26.080
(EXCLAIMING) Eight seconds?
Over there?

467
00:35:26.950 --> 00:35:29.480
Yeah, l just need
a little incentive.

468
00:35:42.430 --> 00:35:43.630
(SIGHS)

469
00:35:49.970 --> 00:35:52.030
Yeah. l can fly.

470
00:35:52.610 --> 00:35:53.700
No!

471
00:35:53.780 --> 00:35:55.340
Can't l do what l want?

472
00:35:55.410 --> 00:35:58.580
l think
you'd be more comfortable
keeping it real.

473
00:35:59.550 --> 00:36:02.750
Think of running fast,
like the Road Runner, okay?

474
00:36:08.230 --> 00:36:09.630
(SNICKERING)

475
00:36:09.930 --> 00:36:11.590
l can handle this.

476
00:36:14.670 --> 00:36:16.260
Adios, muchacho.

477
00:36:18.700 --> 00:36:20.300
Oh, wait! Chris!

478
00:36:20.540 --> 00:36:22.400
Annie!

479
00:36:27.110 --> 00:36:29.600
l bet you're thinking
"Oh, shit!" now!

480
00:36:29.680 --> 00:36:31.050
(SCREAMING)

481
00:36:41.090 --> 00:36:42.460
(SCREAMING)

482
00:36:48.570 --> 00:36:49.800
Yeah!

483
00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:51.230
Go, boy!

484
00:36:51.570 --> 00:36:52.940
(GRUNTING)

485
00:36:54.970 --> 00:36:56.270
(WHOOPING)

486
00:36:57.510 --> 00:36:59.500
Go, Chris, go!

487
00:37:13.060 --> 00:37:14.390
(EXCLAIMS)

488
00:37:25.870 --> 00:37:27.070
Albert!

489
00:37:27.770 --> 00:37:28.970
Albert!

490
00:37:37.850 --> 00:37:39.610
lt's completely new.

491
00:37:40.520 --> 00:37:43.110
The canvas was blank
when l was alive.

492
00:37:44.520 --> 00:37:47.320
How can l see this drawing
after l'm dead?

493
00:37:49.530 --> 00:37:52.220
For an expert
you look pretty surprised.

494
00:37:52.660 --> 00:37:54.630
ALBERT: You two.
A long courtship?

495
00:37:54.700 --> 00:37:55.860
No, actually.

496
00:37:55.930 --> 00:37:57.870
From the first moment,
it was like...

497
00:37:57.940 --> 00:37:59.270
Soul mates.

498
00:37:59.670 --> 00:38:02.110
lt's extremely rare,
but it exists.

499
00:38:03.470 --> 00:38:06.170
Like twin souls.
Tuned in to each other.

500
00:38:08.410 --> 00:38:10.440
Apparently, even in death.

501
00:38:12.780 --> 00:38:15.150
You're reaching each other
through her painting.

502
00:38:15.220 --> 00:38:17.350
lt's nothing l've ever seen.

503
00:38:19.920 --> 00:38:22.260
ANNIE: You can't see it,
can you?

504
00:38:25.160 --> 00:38:26.890
And you never will.

505
00:38:35.440 --> 00:38:36.700
(SIGHING)

506
00:38:37.240 --> 00:38:38.570
(CREAKING)

507
00:39:07.840 --> 00:39:09.330
l love you!

508
00:39:47.510 --> 00:39:49.040
(KATIE BARKING)

509
00:39:55.850 --> 00:39:58.250
CHRIS: Whose footprints
are these?

510
00:39:59.390 --> 00:40:01.620
Don't ask me,
you put 'em here.

511
00:40:05.230 --> 00:40:06.600
(SQUAWKING)

512
00:40:14.170 --> 00:40:15.330
Annie.

513
00:40:16.010 --> 00:40:17.130
Annie!

514
00:40:17.210 --> 00:40:18.970
ALBERT: Chris!
Annie!

515
00:40:26.420 --> 00:40:28.910
Fantasy is not
what you need, Chris.

516
00:40:30.220 --> 00:40:31.850
No, you're right.

517
00:40:32.490 --> 00:40:33.960
l need Annie.

518
00:40:36.530 --> 00:40:37.820
That'll change in time.

519
00:40:37.900 --> 00:40:39.760
Oh, come on, Einstein!

520
00:40:40.060 --> 00:40:42.360
Time's not on my watch
any more!

521
00:40:42.430 --> 00:40:44.420
Time does not exist here!

522
00:40:45.070 --> 00:40:48.840
Wherever it went,
it won't make me
need Annie less.

523
00:40:51.480 --> 00:40:54.040
You'll feel differently,
and so will she.

524
00:40:54.110 --> 00:40:55.170
Man.

525
00:40:57.050 --> 00:40:58.710
You don't know us.

526
00:41:00.320 --> 00:41:01.680
Wish l did.

527
00:41:08.960 --> 00:41:10.120
CHRIS: Marie.

528
00:41:11.300 --> 00:41:12.460
Marie!

529
00:41:18.300 --> 00:41:19.960
Look, it's Tigger!

530
00:41:20.400 --> 00:41:22.130
lt's my daughter's!

531
00:41:23.070 --> 00:41:25.270
Katie tore it up once, and...

532
00:41:29.410 --> 00:41:31.080
She's here, right?

533
00:41:32.220 --> 00:41:33.680
Where is she?

534
00:41:36.290 --> 00:41:39.810
Chris, here is big enough
for all to have
their universe.

535
00:41:42.660 --> 00:41:45.720
That's not why
you haven't seen them yet,
is it?

536
00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:50.130
What does that mean, Buddha?

537
00:41:51.340 --> 00:41:53.630
l wanna see
my children, Albert!

538
00:41:56.140 --> 00:41:58.010
When you do, you will.

539
00:42:15.860 --> 00:42:17.060
Does that hurt?

540
00:42:17.130 --> 00:42:18.360
Mmm-mmm.

541
00:42:19.460 --> 00:42:20.930
That?
Mmm-hmm.

542
00:42:21.770 --> 00:42:23.290
How about that?

543
00:42:23.700 --> 00:42:26.500
l'm gonna keep doing this
till you tickle.

544
00:42:30.940 --> 00:42:33.880
You've got a fever.
lt's going down, though.

545
00:42:34.210 --> 00:42:36.440
Don't you have
to go somewhere?

546
00:42:38.720 --> 00:42:40.340
Wanna play chess?

547
00:42:44.020 --> 00:42:45.680
l could teach you.

548
00:42:47.230 --> 00:42:49.190
Would you teach me that?

549
00:43:18.290 --> 00:43:19.620
Excuse me.

550
00:43:22.530 --> 00:43:24.050
Albert has to work.

551
00:43:24.130 --> 00:43:26.260
He asked me
to meet with you.

552
00:43:27.230 --> 00:43:29.130
Will that be all right?

553
00:43:30.270 --> 00:43:31.500
Leona.

554
00:43:31.900 --> 00:43:33.200
That's a very beautiful name.

555
00:43:33.270 --> 00:43:35.470
He said you've been isolated.

556
00:43:36.910 --> 00:43:39.600
Do you wanna see others?
Perhaps a city?

557
00:43:40.310 --> 00:43:42.910
l would,
but travel makes me nauseous.

558
00:43:45.220 --> 00:43:46.580
(CHUCKLING)

559
00:43:49.650 --> 00:43:51.250
Close your eyes.

560
00:43:53.090 --> 00:43:54.960
l didn't mean forever.

561
00:44:06.240 --> 00:44:07.710
(LEONA LAUGHING)

562
00:44:07.770 --> 00:44:09.430
What do you think?

563
00:44:09.970 --> 00:44:12.070
l'm a little under-dressed.

564
00:44:12.340 --> 00:44:13.830
You look fine.

565
00:44:14.110 --> 00:44:17.550
Till now you've been
painting your world.
This is mine.

566
00:44:18.220 --> 00:44:21.950
ln our city across the river
we have to have
a common vision.

567
00:44:23.550 --> 00:44:25.280
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

568
00:44:25.690 --> 00:44:27.320
(PEOPLE LAUGHING)

569
00:44:38.040 --> 00:44:40.130
So, there's work.

570
00:44:40.640 --> 00:44:42.400
Mmm-hmm.
l like that.

571
00:44:43.110 --> 00:44:46.510
Albert, for example,
is sort of a missionary.

572
00:44:46.780 --> 00:44:48.540
He saves lost souls.

573
00:44:48.610 --> 00:44:49.840
Like me.

574
00:44:50.380 --> 00:44:53.580
Hardly. They are the ones
who can't get here.

575
00:44:55.350 --> 00:44:57.120
You mean, from hell?

576
00:44:57.190 --> 00:44:58.450
ln a way.

577
00:44:58.590 --> 00:45:00.560
lt's not what you think.

578
00:45:00.660 --> 00:45:03.130
My work is with animals.

579
00:45:03.360 --> 00:45:04.620
(BARKING)

580
00:45:05.700 --> 00:45:07.600
Katie is an old friend.

581
00:45:09.130 --> 00:45:11.030
ANNIE: Dearest Christy.

582
00:45:11.540 --> 00:45:14.030
l don't know how
this day unraveled on me.

583
00:45:14.110 --> 00:45:16.570
l was so proud of
how l held together through

584
00:45:16.640 --> 00:45:18.540
this endless afternoon.

585
00:45:19.540 --> 00:45:22.070
But, coming home,
l began to lose it.

586
00:45:24.320 --> 00:45:26.410
lf l had walked out that night
for our Double D,

587
00:45:26.480 --> 00:45:29.850
you wouldn't have been
in the tunnel
doing me a favor.

588
00:45:30.790 --> 00:45:33.220
A whole family lost
in car crashes.

589
00:45:34.490 --> 00:45:36.930
Enough to make a person
buy a bike.

590
00:45:38.630 --> 00:45:39.960
(LAUGHTER)

591
00:45:41.830 --> 00:45:43.060
CHRIS: Where are they going?

592
00:45:43.130 --> 00:45:45.860
LEONA: To help others
be reborn on Earth.

593
00:45:46.170 --> 00:45:48.300
Really? Reincarnation?

594
00:45:50.510 --> 00:45:52.140
(PEOPLE SCATTING)

595
00:45:56.550 --> 00:45:58.680
Albert says to cheer you up.

596
00:45:59.620 --> 00:46:02.520
You have difficulty...
Losing my wife, yeah.

597
00:46:05.490 --> 00:46:07.150
And your children?

598
00:46:07.930 --> 00:46:09.690
They died years ago.

599
00:46:10.130 --> 00:46:12.650
That's why l'm worried
about my wife.

600
00:46:15.300 --> 00:46:17.790
They died
in a terrible collision.

601
00:46:17.870 --> 00:46:19.390
The nanny was driving.

602
00:46:19.470 --> 00:46:21.170
lt wasn't her fault.

603
00:46:21.240 --> 00:46:22.730
And your wife?

604
00:46:23.740 --> 00:46:26.180
My daughter
had asked her to drive.

605
00:46:26.280 --> 00:46:28.010
(CHILDREN LAUGHING)

606
00:46:43.730 --> 00:46:45.720
lt was a trucker's fault.

607
00:46:46.460 --> 00:46:49.560
But my wife believed
that if she'd been driving,

608
00:46:50.170 --> 00:46:52.760
her protective instincts
would have...

609
00:46:55.670 --> 00:46:57.440
(LAUGHTER CONTINUES)

610
00:47:02.310 --> 00:47:03.640
(SCATTING)

611
00:47:05.880 --> 00:47:07.350
Are you okay?

612
00:47:14.430 --> 00:47:15.950
Come on, Katie!

613
00:47:30.240 --> 00:47:32.470
LEONA:
Where were you just now?

614
00:47:33.140 --> 00:47:35.870
Your mind's been wandering
all afternoon.

615
00:47:36.980 --> 00:47:38.740
Thinking of someone.

616
00:47:40.580 --> 00:47:43.750
Your wife must have
loved her children very much.

617
00:47:44.790 --> 00:47:46.120
Very much.

618
00:47:46.820 --> 00:47:50.120
But you don't have to
break in half
to love somebody.

619
00:47:53.430 --> 00:47:55.630
Tell me a memory of your own.

620
00:47:57.540 --> 00:47:59.500
Say, with your daughter.

621
00:48:18.020 --> 00:48:19.290
CHRIS: Hey.

622
00:48:19.360 --> 00:48:21.450
That's somebody else's art.

623
00:48:21.830 --> 00:48:23.690
What's the difference?

624
00:48:24.160 --> 00:48:26.220
You weren't looking anyway.

625
00:48:30.870 --> 00:48:32.200
Your move.

626
00:48:34.410 --> 00:48:36.700
ls this where
we go when we die?

627
00:48:42.580 --> 00:48:45.310
lt's a dream, baby.
lt's a beautiful one.

628
00:48:46.950 --> 00:48:49.850
But, you know, dreams...
l know, aren't real.

629
00:48:50.450 --> 00:48:51.650
l know.

630
00:48:55.490 --> 00:48:57.650
lt's after midnight.
l haven't won yet.

631
00:48:57.730 --> 00:48:58.850
lt's your first time.

632
00:48:58.930 --> 00:49:01.060
No, l like that
l haven't won yet.

633
00:49:01.130 --> 00:49:03.160
Means you're not cheating.

634
00:49:03.800 --> 00:49:05.960
And when l win,
l really win.

635
00:49:07.070 --> 00:49:08.970
l wanna play till l do.

636
00:49:10.040 --> 00:49:11.440
Unless you wanna stop.

637
00:49:11.510 --> 00:49:13.640
No. Let's play till you win.

638
00:49:16.610 --> 00:49:19.050
CHRIS: She died
three months later.

639
00:49:20.020 --> 00:49:21.880
We played every night.

640
00:49:24.620 --> 00:49:26.610
lt meant the world to me.

641
00:49:28.730 --> 00:49:30.220
She never won.

642
00:49:57.890 --> 00:50:00.880
l didn't look like this
in the body, you know.

643
00:50:04.700 --> 00:50:06.720
We flew to Singapore once.

644
00:50:07.030 --> 00:50:10.870
And my daddy smiled at
the flight attendant who

645
00:50:14.410 --> 00:50:17.500
looked like this
and wore this name tag,
"Leona".

646
00:50:17.610 --> 00:50:19.130
(BOTH LAUGHING)

647
00:50:21.110 --> 00:50:23.310
He said Asian women are so

648
00:50:25.280 --> 00:50:28.550
lovely and graceful

649
00:50:30.450 --> 00:50:31.440
and intelligent.

650
00:50:31.520 --> 00:50:33.620
He didn't mean only.
l know.

651
00:50:33.690 --> 00:50:35.450
lt was something he said.

652
00:50:35.530 --> 00:50:39.590
And l thought,
when l grow up,
l wanna be that.

653
00:50:43.200 --> 00:50:45.030
You still play chess?

654
00:50:54.810 --> 00:50:57.110
l think l waited
for my partner.

655
00:51:40.290 --> 00:51:43.730
ANNIE: l swear that California
is the strangest place.

656
00:51:44.660 --> 00:51:46.030
They push you into it

657
00:51:46.100 --> 00:51:49.190
so you can do it before
your shrink commits you.

658
00:51:50.630 --> 00:51:52.830
Thoughtful legislation there.

659
00:51:54.040 --> 00:51:55.770
Mine is suspicious.

660
00:51:56.470 --> 00:51:58.770
Another week,
he might commit me.

661
00:51:58.840 --> 00:52:00.500
For my own safety.

662
00:52:03.710 --> 00:52:06.310
l had the husband
l was meant to have.

663
00:52:06.820 --> 00:52:08.810
Two spectacular children.

664
00:52:09.690 --> 00:52:13.490
Blessings no one would dare
expect from life.

665
00:52:15.390 --> 00:52:17.490
And the truth is, simply

666
00:52:19.700 --> 00:52:21.220
that it's over.

667
00:52:23.070 --> 00:52:26.130
Just this one loose end
to ravel up.

668
00:52:32.140 --> 00:52:35.700
l didn't get to say goodbye.
You're dead and l blew that.

669
00:52:38.850 --> 00:52:40.940
l don't get to say goodbye.

670
00:52:44.050 --> 00:52:45.950
But l'll tell you what.

671
00:52:46.690 --> 00:52:49.280
Across whatever distance
there is,

672
00:52:51.900 --> 00:52:53.630
l send you my love.

673
00:53:08.110 --> 00:53:09.170
Hey.

674
00:53:12.150 --> 00:53:13.510
Where were you?

675
00:53:13.580 --> 00:53:14.850
Far away.

676
00:53:14.920 --> 00:53:17.250
l got called back.
l was working.

677
00:53:19.860 --> 00:53:22.160
There are no words
to thank you.

678
00:53:23.290 --> 00:53:24.950
For finding Marie.

679
00:53:25.060 --> 00:53:26.290
(SIGHS)

680
00:53:28.230 --> 00:53:30.170
ls she okay?
She's fine.

681
00:53:30.630 --> 00:53:32.400
You'll see her soon.

682
00:53:32.670 --> 00:53:34.400
She sends her love.

683
00:53:35.410 --> 00:53:36.930
Especially now.

684
00:53:45.150 --> 00:53:48.520
We'll gonna go through
something very hard right now.

685
00:53:49.190 --> 00:53:51.420
l'm with you.
You're not alone.

686
00:53:54.730 --> 00:53:56.220
Annie is dead.

687
00:54:00.860 --> 00:54:02.590
She killed herself.

688
00:54:07.470 --> 00:54:10.630
lt's nothing l ever expected.

689
00:54:13.680 --> 00:54:15.910
Like l said,
you don't know us.

690
00:54:18.620 --> 00:54:21.450
ls that
an occupational hazard
of soul mates?

691
00:54:21.620 --> 00:54:23.950
One's not much
without the other?

692
00:54:27.360 --> 00:54:28.880
But she's okay.

693
00:54:29.730 --> 00:54:32.090
Because her pain is over.

694
00:54:32.160 --> 00:54:33.190
You don't understand.

695
00:54:33.260 --> 00:54:35.230
She won't cling like me.

696
00:54:35.500 --> 00:54:37.160
When do l see her?

697
00:54:37.300 --> 00:54:38.460
Never.

698
00:54:41.270 --> 00:54:42.970
You'll never see her.

699
00:54:43.040 --> 00:54:45.940
She's a suicide.
Suicides go somewhere else.

700
00:54:46.880 --> 00:54:48.350
Why are you punishing her?

701
00:54:48.410 --> 00:54:50.740
lt's not punishment.
She's suffered enough.

702
00:54:50.810 --> 00:54:52.780
There are no judges
or crimes.

703
00:54:52.850 --> 00:54:54.010
Everybody's equal.

704
00:54:54.080 --> 00:54:55.980
That's the way things work!

705
00:54:56.050 --> 00:54:58.320
And suicides go to hell?

706
00:54:58.590 --> 00:55:00.720
No goddamn judgment in that!

707
00:55:03.630 --> 00:55:05.220
You wanna fight?

708
00:55:06.730 --> 00:55:09.720
You can hide from it
or understand it.

709
00:55:10.670 --> 00:55:14.330
What you call hell
is for those
who don't know they're dead.

710
00:55:14.540 --> 00:55:18.000
They can't realize
what they've done
or what's happened.

711
00:55:19.080 --> 00:55:21.340
Too self-absorbed in life,
that they...

712
00:55:21.410 --> 00:55:22.710
Self-absorbed?

713
00:55:22.780 --> 00:55:25.410
That doesn't apply to Annie,
all right?

714
00:55:26.820 --> 00:55:28.340
No, it doesn't.

715
00:55:28.750 --> 00:55:30.650
Suicides are different.

716
00:55:30.720 --> 00:55:33.210
They don't go to hell
because they're immoral
or selfish.

717
00:55:33.290 --> 00:55:35.730
They go for
a very different reason.

718
00:55:35.790 --> 00:55:40.030
Each of us has an instinct,
and there's a natural order
to ourjourney.

719
00:55:40.160 --> 00:55:42.130
Annie has violated that.

720
00:55:42.700 --> 00:55:44.360
She won't face it.

721
00:55:45.340 --> 00:55:49.270
She won't realize,
accept what she's done.

722
00:55:50.470 --> 00:55:53.200
She will spend eternity
playing that out.

723
00:55:53.340 --> 00:55:55.110
You still say she's in hell.

724
00:55:55.180 --> 00:55:56.240
Everybody's hell
is different.

725
00:55:56.310 --> 00:55:58.180
lt's not all fire and pain.

726
00:55:58.250 --> 00:56:00.680
Real hell
is your life gone wrong.

727
00:56:05.490 --> 00:56:07.150
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

728
00:56:20.440 --> 00:56:22.100
l'm her soul mate.

729
00:56:22.170 --> 00:56:23.700
l can find her.

730
00:56:31.620 --> 00:56:32.950
You don't understand how...

731
00:56:33.020 --> 00:56:35.920
lt's not
about understanding!

732
00:56:36.890 --> 00:56:39.080
lt's about not giving up.

733
00:56:40.720 --> 00:56:42.850
You said there are no rules.

734
00:56:42.930 --> 00:56:44.360
And the purple tree?

735
00:56:44.430 --> 00:56:46.420
You were
pretty surprised then.

736
00:56:46.500 --> 00:56:49.560
(CHUCKLING)
Hey, if there are no rules,

737
00:56:49.770 --> 00:56:52.570
how can you say
all suicides are the same?

738
00:56:52.700 --> 00:56:54.070
l can't, l can't.

739
00:56:54.140 --> 00:56:57.540
Okay. Or she doesn't know
she's dead?

740
00:56:57.610 --> 00:56:58.700
l can't.
Okay.

741
00:56:58.780 --> 00:57:02.370
No one has ever seen
a suicide brought back!

742
00:57:02.450 --> 00:57:03.910
Stick around, Chief.

743
00:57:03.980 --> 00:57:06.070
You ain't seen nothing yet.

744
00:57:12.320 --> 00:57:14.550
Okay.
You deserve your chance.

745
00:57:15.160 --> 00:57:16.960
We'll find a tracker.

746
00:57:24.730 --> 00:57:26.200
(MAN SINGING)

747
00:57:28.710 --> 00:57:30.640
(lNDISTINCT CHATTERING)

748
00:57:42.790 --> 00:57:44.280
(MAN SHOUTING)

749
00:58:18.320 --> 00:58:19.880
(WOMEN SINGING)

750
00:58:24.630 --> 00:58:26.530
(lNDISTINCT CHATTERING)

751
00:58:38.180 --> 00:58:39.570
ALBERT: Hey!

752
00:58:46.720 --> 00:58:49.050
This the guy
who doesn't give up?

753
00:58:50.390 --> 00:58:53.790
Anyone tell you
too much persistence
can get stupid?

754
00:58:54.190 --> 00:58:55.560
Constantly.

755
00:58:55.890 --> 00:58:57.330
l hear the same thing.

756
00:58:57.390 --> 00:58:59.520
l also hear l read too slow.

757
00:59:00.130 --> 00:59:01.930
l don't need glasses.

758
00:59:02.530 --> 00:59:05.160
Eyes being a figment
of my imagination.

759
00:59:06.900 --> 00:59:09.370
You'll hear a lot
of smart stuff here.

760
00:59:09.440 --> 00:59:11.030
lt's usually right.

761
00:59:11.110 --> 00:59:12.370
Don't let it screw you up.

762
00:59:12.440 --> 00:59:13.670
l won't.

763
00:59:14.840 --> 00:59:17.040
Your wife love you as strong?

764
00:59:25.620 --> 00:59:27.150
We'll find her.

765
00:59:27.990 --> 00:59:29.790
But when you find her,

766
00:59:30.560 --> 00:59:33.050
nothing will make her
recognize you.

767
00:59:34.000 --> 00:59:36.230
Nothing will break her denial.

768
00:59:37.400 --> 00:59:39.530
lt's stronger than her love.

769
00:59:39.900 --> 00:59:42.200
ln fact,
reinforced by her love.

770
00:59:43.870 --> 00:59:46.500
You can say everything
you long to say.

771
00:59:47.440 --> 00:59:49.110
lncluding goodbye.

772
00:59:49.610 --> 00:59:51.910
Even if she
can't understand it.

773
00:59:53.680 --> 00:59:57.050
You'll have the satisfaction
that you didn't give up.

774
00:59:59.490 --> 01:00:01.360
That has to be enough.

775
01:00:01.890 --> 01:00:04.420
Get me there.
l decide what's enough.

776
01:00:06.830 --> 01:00:08.460
When do we leave?

777
01:00:10.370 --> 01:00:11.960
Close your eyes.

778
01:00:23.780 --> 01:00:25.750
CHRIS: Albert's a sweet kid.

779
01:00:25.820 --> 01:00:27.580
TRACKER: He is that.

780
01:00:27.850 --> 01:00:30.650
There's a tenderness
l never knew in life.

781
01:00:31.050 --> 01:00:33.550
l didn't know him
when he was young.

782
01:00:35.290 --> 01:00:37.590
Were you proud
of your own kids?

783
01:00:39.600 --> 01:00:40.930
Of course.

784
01:00:41.430 --> 01:00:44.260
That's an easy
bullshit answer.

785
01:00:45.900 --> 01:00:47.430
Think about it.

786
01:00:49.370 --> 01:00:51.100
l said "Of course."

787
01:00:52.880 --> 01:00:54.780
l like this sore point.

788
01:00:55.080 --> 01:00:57.840
lts juice... Juice is strong.
lt connects.

789
01:00:59.150 --> 01:01:01.740
Makes you a better receiver
for Annie.

790
01:01:04.990 --> 01:01:08.220
She's the transmitter,
sending thoughts of you.

791
01:01:11.560 --> 01:01:12.820
(GASPING)

792
01:01:32.580 --> 01:01:34.710
What did you do when alive?

793
01:01:34.880 --> 01:01:36.780
You mean the last time?

794
01:01:37.090 --> 01:01:39.720
We can be reborn.

795
01:01:39.820 --> 01:01:41.810
But only if we choose to.

796
01:01:43.330 --> 01:01:45.590
Last trip,
l did the same work...

797
01:01:45.660 --> 01:01:47.320
You were a shrink!

798
01:01:48.400 --> 01:01:50.060
Fairly perceptive.

799
01:01:56.240 --> 01:01:57.600
Oh, my God.

800
01:01:58.110 --> 01:02:00.300
You expected physical danger?

801
01:02:01.380 --> 01:02:03.040
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

802
01:02:05.420 --> 01:02:07.750
What could it do,
kill you, huh?

803
01:02:08.050 --> 01:02:11.280
No. ln hell,
there's real danger.

804
01:02:12.860 --> 01:02:14.620
Of losing your mind.

805
01:02:15.990 --> 01:02:17.360
(SCREAMING)

806
01:02:54.760 --> 01:02:57.930
ANNIE: Because he's drowning,
that's why.

807
01:03:02.110 --> 01:03:04.600
He's 13 years old!

808
01:03:04.670 --> 01:03:05.660
CHRIS: l know.

809
01:03:05.740 --> 01:03:08.110
He needs to hang out
with his friends.
That's what he needs.

